/F 768
/FT /Btn
/Ff 65536
/H /N
/Rect [72.414 426.303 537.402 745.293]
/Subtype /Widget
/T (tooltip zref@3)
/TU (Framework outlining the sustainability implications of core emerging technologies in the ASM \(Adaptive Social Manufacturing\) framework, categorised into economic, environmental, and social impacts. Technologies include Artificial Intelligence, Intelligent Automation, Cognitive Cyber-Physical Systems, and Extended Reality. Positive impacts \(in green boxes\) cover areas such as efficiency, productivity, renewable energy integration, improved work-life balance, and enhanced job roles. Negative impacts \(in red boxes\) highlight concerns like increased energy consumption, e-waste generation, system complexity, job displacement, and potential privacy risks. Each technology has distinct positive and negative implications across economic, environmental, and social dimensions, contributing to both benefits and challenges in sustainable manufacturing.)
/Type /Annot
>>
